{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\ndocs/README.md currently combines audience routing, document summaries, taxonomy policy, troubleshooting, generated-artifact ownership, and historical evidence. F01 moves policy and generated ownership to canonical pages. F06 can then make this file one compact landing page without losing discovery paths.\n\n## Current enforcement and history\n\nTicket mucky-like-elkhound added the docs index and scripts/check_docs_index.py. The checker requires every maintained top-level docs Markdown page to appear as a link target. It does not classify pages by audience and does not detect duplicate directory entries. The current landing page also states that ticket links have six relations and that some ADR numbers are shared. Current ticket-model and ADR index behavior no longer supports those statements.\n\n## Plan\n\nRewrite only docs/README.md. Provide labeled routes for clients, contributors, architecture readers, ADR readers, operators, research readers, and evidence readers. Preserve direct discovery for CLI use, MCP use, project adoption, contribution, and internals. Preserve the three existing troubleshooting rows and their remedies. Add one compact directory that links every maintained top-level docs Markdown page exactly once and classifies it under one route. Link subdirectory indexes where they are the correct entry point. Keep the generated inventory on docs/generated-artifacts.md.\n\nRetain bash-migration.md, 88ab-feature-branch-evidence.md, and dco-rollout-evidence.md at their existing paths and list each exactly once as historical evidence. Remove the outdated six-relation statement and the claim that ADR numbers remain shared.\n\n## Exclusions\n\n- No content edits outside docs/README.md.\n- No file relocation or deletion.\n- No generated catalog on the landing page.\n- No new validation behavior. F07 owns validation after this structure lands.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] docs/README.md provides distinct client, contributor, architecture, ADR, operations, research, and evidence routes.\n- [x] The landing page preserves discoverable paths for CLI use, MCP use, adoption, contribution, and internals.\n- [x] The compact directory links every maintained top-level docs Markdown page exactly once.\n- [x] The three existing troubleshooting rows and their remedies remain present.\n- [x] bash-migration.md, 88ab-feature-branch-evidence.md, and dco-rollout-evidence.md remain at their current paths and each appears once in the directory.\n- [x] The landing page contains no generated-artifact tables, no six-relation claim, and no claim that ADR numbers remain shared.\n- [x] scripts/check_docs_index.py --check, make lint, make typecheck, and the project test gate pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787375616223864001,"uuid":"301bba49-df31-4d6c-bd7d-5a6842b6c2a7"}